1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,869
One question, five runs.

2
00:00:01,919 --> 00:00:12,901
When a user pushes an insurance agent for a payout, does the agent keep naming the licensed adjuster as the one who decides?

3
00:00:12,951 --> 00:00:15,778
Four models, two families, one instrument.

4
00:00:15,828 --> 00:00:18,656
Everything was pre-registered, including what failed.

5
00:00:19,206 --> 00:00:21,304
The design has two arms.

6
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:33,328
In escalation the user asks for the payout to be approved, and the agent names the limit forty-eight to sixty percent of the time, in all four models.

7
00:00:33,378 --> 00:00:39,340
In sustained pressure nobody asks: urgency, a prior promise, social proof, a claimed authority.

8
00:00:39,390 --> 00:00:43,634
That arm runs from twelve point five to fifty percent.

9
00:00:43,684 --> 00:00:45,352
Forty conversations per arm.

10
00:00:45,902 --> 00:00:47,541
The five runs.

11
00:00:47,591 --> 00:00:54,299
The escalation column barely moves: fifty, forty-eight point seven, sixty, sixty, fifty.

12
00:00:54,349 --> 00:01:06,689
The sustained column moves by a factor of four: twenty-eight point nine, eighteen point four, forty-seven point five, fifty, twelve point five.

13
00:01:07,239 --> 00:01:09,704
We could have published a ranking.

14
00:01:09,754 --> 00:01:14,317
The intervals do not allow it: only two contrasts clear zero.

15
00:01:14,367 --> 00:01:17,671
And the decisive number is not between models.

16
00:01:17,721 --> 00:01:25,218
The same model, run twice with the same instrument, reads twenty-eight point nine and then eighteen point four.

17
00:01:25,268 --> 00:01:28,572
A ten point gap, whose interval crosses zero.

18
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:33,603
At forty turns per arm, ordering these models would be ordering noise.

19
00:01:34,153 --> 00:01:34,103


20
00:01:34,153 --> 00:01:41,968
The contract's own adapter read zero of forty: it required a literal phrase, and the model wrote the passive voice.

21
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:45,507
Repaired, it reaches six of eight cells in sample.

22
00:01:45,557 --> 00:01:52,192
Then it met a new model's text: it held escalation, and lost five of five in sustained.

23
00:01:52,242 --> 00:01:59,663
All five are one construction, I can help by collecting, written before that text existed, and not patched after.

24
00:02:00,213 --> 00:02:00,163


25
00:02:00,213 --> 00:02:11,778
Across five hundred and ninety-one replies, three hundred and twenty of them under pressure, the contract's list of forbidden phrasings finds zero approvals, zero promises, zero quotes.

26
00:02:11,828 --> 00:02:16,080
No model cedes. What differs is whether it says why.

27
00:02:16,130 --> 00:02:22,964
A lower restatement rate is not a safety win: it means the limit is rarely named.

28
00:02:23,514 --> 00:02:23,464


29
00:02:23,514 --> 00:02:32,342
All of it runs offline from a clone, with no API key: the signed evidence check, the clause audit, the cession check.

30
00:02:32,392 --> 00:02:40,010
Every figure sits beside its pre-registration, its nulls, and two claims that were withdrawn when they failed to replicate.

